WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.037
Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis on his maiden voyage to Iowa.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.941
I bring greetings
from the free state of Florida,

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:11.444
riding a wave of lofty expectation
as to the state that opens

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.347
the Republican presidential contest
in less than a year.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.448
People lined up

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:19.352
to catch a glimpse of the governor
who technically is promoting his book.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.723
This is the number one bestselling
nonfiction book in the country, but

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:27.761
actually is testing a White House bid that
he intends to make official by summer.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.963
Welcome to Iowa. This is your first trip.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:34.434
DeSantis has told advisers he will wait
until the Florida legislative session ends

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.470
so he can campaign on an even bolder
agenda,

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.940
one that is delighting supporters
and alarming critics.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:45.512
I always tell my legislators,
you watch Iowa, watch to watch these.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.181
Do not let them get ahead of us
on any of this stuff.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.683
So we've got our legislature here
in session now.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:51.451
So buckle up.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:54.421
The next 60 days should be fine
in Florida.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.223
He's stoking the culture wars in schools.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.394
We're also leading on ensuring
that our school system

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:07.534
is focusing on educating our kids,
not indoctrinating our kids and beyond.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.768
We've got to fight.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:12.572
If we see it in medicine,
or the universities or the corporations,

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.341
you can't just say Let it go,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:19.412
because then we're going to be living
under an oppressive woke ocracy

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:23.049
holding up his Florida record
as a blueprint for a national platform

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:26.553
and presenting himself as a doer,
not a talker.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.456
A leader is not captive to polls.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:32.158
We don't have palace intrigue.
We don't have any drama.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.161
It's just execution every single day.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.231
I'll build the wall
myself. I'll do it this.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.366
Let me add him we'll get it done.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.703
That was a subtle yet unmistakable
distinction with Donald Trump,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.139
who visits Iowa on Monday.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:50.343
The 2024 Republican campaign
is intensifying with former South

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:54.581
Carolina Governor Nikki Haley
urging Iowa voters to keep an open mind.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.883
Whatever the polls tell you today,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.053
that is not where the polls
are going to be a year from now.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.990
But for many Republicans, the Florida
governor stands as a beacon of hope

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:07.560
for those who admire Trump
but are eager to move on.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.863
I would love to have him
as our next president.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.497
Becky Grist.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:13.333
Bock was among those eager to see DeSantis
close up.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.202
President
Trump has been an amazing president,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:20.974
but he alienates too many people
with what he says.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.077
And I think Governor DeSantis

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:27.447
is doing a good job at appealing to

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.283
Americans

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:35.588
Now, the Florida governor just finished
shaking hands here and left the room.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.725
And Erin, I can tell you
Republican had had high expectations

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.362
coming into this day and they are leaving
it having those expectations met.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.765
One Republican voter here
who said they're looking for a change

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:49.335
described the Florida governor
as very impressive, a straight shooter.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.705
Of course, this is probably
the easiest trip he will take to Iowa.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.741
He had no arrows coming his direction.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:58.111
He's heading to Nevada tomorrow,
another early voting state.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:01.614
Of course, this is all before he decides
or announces that he's going to run.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:06.119
But I am told that is expected to come
in May or early June.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:09.856
Carson, we heard Governor Sanders take
a thinly veiled shot at former president

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.524
say when he talks
about how there's no drama

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.360
in his administration,
something he said before.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.762
How long do you think it is

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:19.532
before the tension between the two of them
actually becomes more direct

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.035
Well, I

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:25.271
mean, obviously, Donald Trump
has been openly attacking him.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.909
And the question is how much Ron DeSantis
wants to really seriously engage

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:30.276
with that.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:34.747
I don't think it's really in his interest
to do that because I think we've seen

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.952
in the past what happens to people
who get in the mud with with Donald Trump.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:42.722
You know, they ended up they end up
usually not coming out, looking not great.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:47.694
And he's smarter, I think, to stay focused
on whatever issues it is

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:51.831
that he thinks are going to help him
win the nomination, which is the

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:55.768
if he decides to run, which let's face it,
he's in Iowa in early March.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.704
He lives in Florida.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:00.707
He's probably pretty serious
thinking about running for president.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.076
That's what he's going to do.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:07.313
Then he should just focus more
on the issues that he has

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.414
that excite the base.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.482
Scott, there was reporting today

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.652
by Politico about how many of the other
Republican presidential candidates

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:16.122
both declared an undeclared hour,
focused on attacking Trump and DeSantis.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:19.492
Their thinking is reportedly
that there's only one viable lane

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:22.662
for the anti-Trump vote, and therefore
they need to take the fight to dissenters.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:23.963
Do you agree with that?

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.198
I do.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.233
I think in this primary you've got Trump

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:27.600
and then there's

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.371
going to be one other person that emerges
and right now, if you look at DeSantis

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.872
favorability ratings

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.974
and really look at the fact
that he has virtually

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:38.878
no detractors inside the Republican Party,
every other Republican candidate

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:42.115
who wants this thing is going to have
to find a way to drag him down.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.917
I don't know how they're going to be able
to do it, to be honest.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:45.885
I'm sure they're going to try.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:49.055
But he is in a different universe,
really, than every other person.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.424
That's not Trump
that's seeking this nomination.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:56.963
DeSantis has the right emotional
sort of attachment to the Republican base.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:00.867
And what you see in his favorability
numbers is not only good numbers

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:04.270
among people who voted for Trump,
but also those college educated

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.040
Republican voters that drifted away
from the Republican Party

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.274
and drifted away from Trump.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.309
They love DeSantis.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.377
And so of everybody in this thing
right now,

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.245
he looks like the one

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.213
that has the capability
of putting together

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:17.183
the coalition that could possibly
possibly, I say, topple

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.451
the former president.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.353
He's obviously
never run a national campaign.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:23.523
Kirsten DeSantis, his allies, some of them
arguing his successes, not necessarily

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.591
because of how he campaigns,
but how he governs.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.593
I don't know if that's
sort of laying groundwork for saying he's

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:31.798
not maybe a great national campaigner,
but that obviously remains to be seen.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:35.168
Is that going to be enough in a state
like Iowa where retail politics

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:35.835
are so important?

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.371
Well, we don't really

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:42.141
know whether he's going to be a good
go to national politics or not.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.409
Obviously, there are plenty of people

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.812
who haven't done it before
and have been successful.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:49.615
So, I mean, Donald Trump
never had ever held office at all.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:54.654
So I think we have to wait and see how he
he does on a national stage.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:58.324
And the fact is,
I think if the vote was taken today,

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:03.763
most of the parties is with Donald Trump,
but his numbers are on the downswing.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.399
I mean, they're definitely they used to be

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:10.303
And so there is an opening for a Trump
plus not.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.841
Know, I think there's this idea of also
the people who are a little bit of less of

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.109
of the Trumpian US

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:19.412
I don't think there's much appetite
for that in the Republican Party.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:23.716
They're looking for either a Trump or
a Trump plus a DeSantis is a Trump plus.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.919
It's got you know, I think Democrats
are kind of betting that Governor

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:31.591
DeSantis, his focus on culture wars
will turn off women working class voters.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:35.027
Do you think moderate swing
state voters care very much when he boasts

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:37.630
that Florida is where vote goes to die?
You think that plays well?

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.634
Well, I mean, the only evidence
I have to look at on this is what happened

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.737
in his reelection campaign in Florida,
that he won by 20 points.

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:47.440
Urban, suburban rural, exurban

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.644
people with college degrees, people
without college degrees, independents.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.279
I mean, women, men.

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:55.982
I mean, any way you slice and dice
humanity, Ron

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:59.552
DeSantis did a pretty darned
good job of racking up votes in Florida.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:01.921
So I think the message he's been running
on, you know,

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:04.524
we've had one test case for it
and it seemed to work.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:08.361
I'll tell you, Anderson, the average
Republican feels surrounded right now.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:11.764
They feel like every large information
distribution information

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:16.002
hub in our society
is really at odds with their worldview,

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:18.538
whether it's corporations,
universities, media,

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.808
you name it, politicians,
government institutions.

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:22.508
And they feel like

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:26.078
DeSantis is the person
who does more than just complain about it.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.114
He actually finishes the fights.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.249
I think that's the line of demarcation
for him.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.518
Everybody in this field can complain.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.519
I can finish it.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.254
You know,
I ask the security and I just want to

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:39.392
I wanted to ask you, Scott,
do you think these candidates know?

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:43.396
I mean, do you think the world knows
how to campaign against Donald Trump

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:44.997
from a Republican standpoint?

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:45.932
Because, I mean,

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:49.435
here we are all these years later
and we're still talking about Will.

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.405
Should Ron DeSantis directly
attack him or not?

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:55.441
We have a whole field of defeated
candidates.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.710
You know, Jeb Bush among them,
Marco Rubio,

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:59.912
who tried all different
ways and none of it worked.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:02.381
Now, I think all the

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:06.886
Republicans from 2016 forward are like
the Will Smith character and I am legend.

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:10.356
They're in the lab and they're like
testing all the theories, the serums out

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.326
and the rats keep dying like
they can't figure out how to solve it.

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.395
Maybe, maybe Ron
DeSantis is the one to solve it.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:21.234
But we don't know yet because the theory
he's going to test out is to put results

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:26.072
up against rhetoric and to put a younger
generation up against an older generation.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:28.908
We just haven't seen this
particular concoction yet.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:30.409
Maybe we'll put it in the lab in Iowa

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:32.912
or New Hampshire or other places,
and it will work.

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:35.948
But but no, no one has
successfully campaigned against him yet

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.383
except one person.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:40.353
And that was Joe Biden
who defeated Donald Trump.

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:41.454
And we know what will happen.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:43.289
I think as a Republican,
I know what will happen

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:44.790
if we nominate Donald Trump again.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.226
Kirsten,
if my memory of the ending of I Am Legend,

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:49.562
I don't want to give away for anybody
who might want to watch it on television,

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:52.164
but it doesn't end well for Will Smith
at the end of the movie.

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:56.769
Is there a right way for DeSantis
to respond to Trump when he decides to?

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:01.374
I don't think it's a good idea
to get into it with Donald Trump.

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:04.644
I think you know, don't let Donald Trump
say what he's going to say.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:07.413
But trying to get, as I said,
trying to get into the mode with him

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:09.515
is not ever going to work
well for anybody.

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:13.352
I think it's better for him to
you know, to respond

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:17.223
