they don't really like that much.

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.532
Right. A lot of times they're like this.

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:29.001
We don't really need this.
Not really adding a lot.

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:31.904
All the little nicknames that you give
everybody so,

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:35.942
you know, but he's going to
you know, he's already going after him.

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:37.343
He needs a better nickname.

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.177
Let's be honest.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:41.581
I don't think the sanctimonious
is probably going to do it,

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:44.750
but he's he's
going to continue to go after him.

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:49.155
But I do think that Ron DeSantis
is qualitatively different

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:52.091
than the other people that I don't know
what Scott thinks about this.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:54.527
But then from the other people that

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:57.630
ran the last time, I think
he's a different kind of politician

00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:00.466
and it is a little more connected
with the base.

00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:02.702
Yeah. Scott Jennings
can totally agree with that. Yeah.

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.937
Yeah,
she what she what she just said, Anderson.

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:06.138
100% correct.

00:10:06.138 --> 00:10:08.874
People are trying to compare him
to the candidates in 2016.

00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:13.079
His numbers and his connection
with Republicans is vastly different

00:10:13.079 --> 00:10:14.413
